ld #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_bead_types.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/task_bead_types.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-p3[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-p3/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task type on the bead wire and store[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-bead-wire[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-bead-wire: add optional `task_type` and `task_type_fields` to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead wire, reducer, and SQLite mirror in sase-core, with cross-field and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]slug-shape validation but no membership list.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task-type spec validation, digest, and body rendering in Rust[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-type-spec[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-bead-wire[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-type-spec: add the task-type spec wire, its validators, its stable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]digest, field-value validation, body-template rendering, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]committed snapshot format to sase-core.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Required plugin prefix for every `use:` field[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]use-prefix[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]use-prefix: require `<plugin>@<id>` on artifact-ref and file-hook `use:`[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]values, migrate every in-tree and chezmoi-managed config, and report [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]legacy bare values as hard errors.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Required-plugin project config and graded enforcement[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]plugins-required[dim] · [dim][/dim]after use-prefix[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugins-required: add the `plugins.required` project config section, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolve it against installed distributions, cross-check it against [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`<plugin>@` prefixes, and enforce it differently per surface.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task-type discovery, catalog assembly, and diagnostics[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]registry[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-type-spec, plugins-required[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]registry: add the `sase_task_types` hookspec and entry-point group, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project-config source, and the central validator that turns discovered [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]specs into one deduplicated catalog with provenance and diagnostics.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Builtin task types and the `sase bead task-type` command group[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]builtins[dim] · [dim][/dim]after registry[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]builtins: author the bug, ci, feature, flake, and memory builtin specs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and expose the catalog through a `sase bead task-type` group.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Typed task creation, field values, and the rendered body block[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]create[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-bead-wire, builtins[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]create: extend the `-T` grammar to `task(<slug>)`, add repeatable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`-f/--field` values, validate them, render the body block below the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]description, and add task-type filters to reading surfaces.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task-type chips on every bead surface[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]presentation[dim] · [dim][/dim]after create[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation: add the shared task-type presentation module with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]distinct accent per type and route every CLI, ACE, bead-page, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-preview, and helper surface through it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Per-type corroboration thresholds[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]triage[dim] · [dim][/dim]after create[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]triage: make the `+1` bar a per-type value with a spec default of zero, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]keep the global knob for untyped legacy beads, and thread it through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every triage and stale-cleanup consumer.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Committed catalog snapshot and the generated task-type memory[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]note[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]snapshot-memory[dim] · [dim][/dim]after builtins[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]snapshot-memory: write `sase/task_types.json` from `sase memory init`, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]render a new generated short memory note from it, move the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]discovered-work instructions into that note, and update the new-task [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]skill.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Missing-plugin gate offering to install[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]install-offer[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plugins-required[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]install-offer: raise one gate per project whose required plugins are [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]missing, offering to install them interactively while agent contexts [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]still fail closed.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The `github` task type and mirror wiring[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]github-type[dim] · [dim][/dim]after registry, create[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]github-type: register the agent-uncreatable `github` task type from the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-github plugin and have the external issue mirror stamp it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make `task_type` required end to end[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]enforce[dim] · [dim][/dim]after create, presentation, triage, snapshot-memory, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]github-type[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]enforce: flip task creation to require a type in both the Rust core and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the CLI once every teaching and rendering surface is in place.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  14 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation, glossary, and end-to-end verification[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]docs-verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after install-offer, enforce[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs-verify: document the registry and required-plugin config, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glossary terms, and verify the whole feature end to end.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-p3","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-p3.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-2819f8dbc2902ceb348c6bb4073916e0","star